"Google I/O 2026: News and announcements (https://blog.google/innovation-and-ai/technology/developers-tools/google-io-2026-collection/)\nciteturn41126search0 [wordlim: 200] Published: 5 months ago; Crawled: 2 weeks ago; May 19, 2026 ... We’re releasing two new models, Gemini Omni and Gemini 3.5.\n\nImage: I/O logo\n\nMay 19, 2026\n\n# I/O 2026\n\n* * *\n\nAt Google I/O 2026, we shared how we’re making AI more helpful for everyone.\n\nWe’re releasing two new models, Gemini Omni and Gemini 3.5. Gemini Omni can create anything from any input, starting with video, and is a leap forward in world understanding, multimodality and editing, while Gemini 3.5 Flash is the first in our latest family of models combining frontier intelligence with action.\n\nWith advancements to Google Antigravity, our agent-first development platform, we’ve moved beyond AI tools that just help us write, to agents that help us act. Thanks to these agents, now anyone can be a builder.\n\nWe’re unlocking agents and agentic experiences across our products — like with Information agents in Search, Gemini Spark and Daily Brief in the Gemini app and the launch of Universal Cart, a truly intelligent shopping cart.\n\nAnd we’re continuing to scale Gemini across our products as well, from Google Pics to intelligent eyewear to Ask YouTube, creating new experiences and expanding to new form factors.\n\nRead on to learn more about what’s new.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nIntroducing Gemini Omni for Google Flow and Flow Music (https://blog.google/innovation-and-ai/models-and-research/google-labs/flow-updates/)\nciteturn41126search1 [wordlim: 200] Published: 5 months ago; Crawled: 2 weeks ago; # New agents, mobile apps and Gemini Omni for Google Flow and Google Flow MusicMay 19, 2026 ...   * Create music videos with Gemini Omni: Our newest model is also coming to Google Flow Music, allowing you to work conversationally with the agent to direct shareable music videos.\n\n# New agents, mobile apps and Gemini Omni for Google Flow and Google Flow Music\n\nMay 19, 2026\n\n|\n\n4 min read\n\nAll new capabilities for the Google Flow family of products help you imagine, collaborate and refine at every stage of your project.\n\nElias Roman VP, Product, Google Labs\n\n* * *\n\nImage: Image with the words: Amplify your vision and unlock your best work.\n\nOn last year’s I/O stage, we introduced Google Flow, built with and for filmmakers. Since then we expanded Flow into an AI creative studio, with new capabilities in video and image generation and editing, and launched in over 140 countries around the world. Earlier this year we added a new tool to our Google Flow family, Google Flow Music, which brings Google’s newest music model, Lyria 3 Pro, to artists, producers and songwriters. We’re now bringing an agent for every step of the creative process, a new AI model that offers precise video editing, the ability to “vibe code” bespoke workflows and mobile applications for on-the-go creation.\n\n## What’s new for Google Flow\n\nWe're taking Google Flow to a new level with Gemini Omni, a new agentic experience and custom tools.\n\n  * Use the full potential of Gemini Omni: Gemini Omni Flash is a model that can create anything from any input, starting with video. It combines Gemini’s intelligence with our generative media models — and is a leap forward in world understanding, multimodality and precise video editing. You can think of Omni like Nano Banana, but for video. For creatives using Google Flow, Omni Flash allows you to blend real-world inspiration with generated content and iterate conversationally. Omni Flash also improves character consistency, meaning identity and voice are preserved across every scene. Omni Flash is available in Flow to Google AI subscribers globally.\n\nSorry, your browser doesn't support embedded videos, but don't worry, you can download it and watch it with your favorite video player!\n\n  * Collaborate at every stage: Google Flow Agent is your creative partner that can plan and reason through complex tasks with your inputs, under your control. Built with Gemini models, it brings expertise and a deep understanding of your project to help with early brainstorming, creating and editing. For example, the agent can be a sounding board for dialogue between characters in a specific scene, or even make plot recommendations. When you’re deeper in a project, your agent can help create multiple variations at one time to give you more options, and even batch edit, so your tweaks are reflected across all your assets. Once you have your assets, your agent can organize them into collections, and it can even intuitively rename them. The agent is now available to all Google Flow users globally.\n\nSorry, your browser doesn't support embedded videos, but don't worry, you can download it and watch it with your favorite video player!\n\n  * Build what you need with bespoke Tools: With Google Flow Tools, you can now use natural language to create bespoke tools and workflows in Google Flow. Whether you’re looking for a particular image editor, video resizer or custom shaders, you can now easily develop them, no coding experience required. And if you create something you think others might like, you can easily share your tool with other Flow users, who can remix it into their own. For example, one of our early access partners László Gaal created a tool called “pixelBento” to apply post-processing effects like lo-fi and glitch aesthetics. Check out this and other Tools, including some from our partners Kat Zhang and metapuppet in Flow. All Flow users globally are able to use existing Tools, while Google AI subscribers can also create and remix them.\n\nSorry, your browser doesn't support embedded videos, but don't worry, you can download it and watch it with your favorite video player!\n\n## What’s new for Google Flow Music\n\nGoogle Flow Music has always allowed you to create, iterate and share studio-quality songs. Our latest features provide more powerful editing control and improved music video creation.\n\nSorry, your browser doesn't support embedded videos, but don't worry, you can download it and watch it with your favorite video player!\n\n  * Precisely edit your song, section by section: We’re giving artists, songwriters and producers more granular control over what they create in Google Flow Music. Now you can highlight any part of a song and make changes. Instantly rewrite or translate lyrics, restyle the beat drop and more — without altering the rest of your track. Or you can sample a specific section of one of your songs, and extend it into a completely different direction.\n  * Reimagine your full tracks with covers: Transform the style of full songs you make in Google Flow Music, while keeping the original melody and structure. For instance, try creating a “lo-fi study” version of your favorite playlist.\n  * Create music videos with Gemini Omni: Our newest model is also coming to Google Flow Music, allowing you to work conversationally with the agent to direct shareable music videos. With Omni Flash you can guide the styles, subjects and scenes to match the narrative and pacing of your track. This is available to all Google AI subscribers.\n\nAnd, for both Google Flow and Google Flow Music, we’re launching mobile apps. While the web versions remain the go-to platforms for access to all capabilities and features, the mobile apps provide flexibility to create on the go. For those 18+, the Flow app is available on Android in beta (iOS coming soon), and the Flow Music app is available now on iOS (Android coming soon).\n\nMillions of creatives across a wide range of disciplines have brought their ideas to life using Google Flow and Google Flow Music in the last year; we can’t wait to see what gets created with these new capabilities in creatives’ hands.\n\nPosted in:\n\n  * Google Labs\n\n* * *\n\nMore Information\n\n* * *\n\n1\n\nFeatures may vary by Google AI subscription tier, platform (web vs. mobile), and region. 18+.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nGoogle I/O 2026: News and announcements (https://blog.google/innovation-and-ai/technology/developers-tools/google-io-2026-collection/?trk=public_post_comment-text)\nciteturn41126search2 [wordlim: 200] Published: 5 months ago; Crawled: 2 weeks ago; May 19, 2026 ... We’re releasing two new models, Gemini Omni and Gemini 3.5.\n\nImage: I/O logo\n\nMay 19, 2026\n\n# I/O 2026\n\n* * *\n\nAt Google I/O 2026, we shared how we’re making AI more helpful for everyone.\n\nWe’re releasing two new models, Gemini Omni and Gemini 3.5. Gemini Omni can create anything from any input, starting with video, and is a leap forward in world understanding, multimodality and editing, while Gemini 3.5 Flash is the first in our latest family of models combining frontier intelligence with action.\n\nWith advancements to Google Antigravity, our agent-first development platform, we’ve moved beyond AI tools that just help us write, to agents that help us act. Thanks to these agents, now anyone can be a builder.\n\nWe’re unlocking agents and agentic experiences across our products — like with Information agents in Search, Gemini Spark and Daily Brief in the Gemini app and the launch of Universal Cart, a truly intelligent shopping cart.\n\nAnd we’re continuing to scale Gemini across our products as well, from Google Pics to intelligent eyewear to Ask YouTube, creating new experiences and expanding to new form factors.\n\nRead on to learn more about what’s new.\n\n  * AI\n\nI/O 2026: Welcome to the agentic Gemini era\n\nBy Sundar Pichai CEO of Google and Alphabet\n\nRead article\n\n  * Gemini models\n\nIntroducing Gemini Omni\n\nBy Koray Kavukcuoglu CTO, Google DeepMind and Chief AI Architect, Google\n\nRead article\n\n  * Gemini App\n\nThe Gemini app becomes more agentic, delivering proactive, 24/7 help\n\nBy Josh Woodward VP, Google Labs, Gemini app & AI Studio\n\nRead article\n\n  * AI\n\n100 things we announced at I/O 2026\n\nBy News from Google Team\n\nRead article\n\n  * Gemini 3.5: frontier intelligence with action\n\nRead article\n\n  * Search\n\nA new era for AI Search\n\nBy Elizabeth Reid VP, Search\n\nRead article\n\n  * Shopping\n\nIntroducing the Universal Cart and more ways to help you shop\n\nBy Vidhya Srinivasan VP/GM Ads and Commerce\n\nRead article\n\n  * Android\n\nIntelligent eyewear is coming this fall\n\nBy Shahram Izadi VP & GM, XR\n\nRead article\n\n  * Google Workspace\n\nNew ways to create and get things done in Google Workspace\n\nBy Yulie Kwon Kim VP, Product, Google Workspace\n\nRead article\n\n  * AI Products\n\nMaking it easier to understand how content was created and edited\n\nBy Laurie Richardson Vice President, Trust & Safety\n\nRead article\n\n  * Google Labs\n\nNew agents, mobile apps and Gemini Omni for Google Flow products\n\nBy Elias Roman VP, Product, Google Labs\n\nRead article\n\n  * NotebookLM\n\nDive deeper into I/O 2026 with NotebookLM.\n\nRead article\n\n  * AI\n\nTake our I/O 2026 quiz, vibe coded in Google AI Studio.\n\nBy Zahra Thompson Contributing writer\n\nRead article\n\n  * AI\n\nHow we used Gemini to build Google I/O 2026\n\nBy Marvin Chow VP, Marketing\n\nRead article\n\n  * Gemini models\n\n9 demos of Gemini Omni and Gemini 3.5 in action\n\nBy Zahra Thompson Contributing writer\n\nRead article\n\n  * AI\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nThe Gemini app becomes more agentic, delivering proactive, 24/7 help (https://blog.google/innovation-and-ai/products/gemini-app/next-evolution-gemini-app/)\nciteturn41126search3 [wordlim: 200] Published: 5 months ago; Crawled: 3 weeks ago; May 19, 2026 ... With Gemini Omni, video editing becomes a fluid, natural conversation. ... Gemini Omni begins rolling out today to Google AI Plus, Pro and Ultra subscribers worldwide.\n\nThe Gemini app becomes more agentic, delivering proactive, 24/7 help\n\n[]\n\n[Input: ]\n\nPreferences\n\n  * [Select]\n\nLinks\n\n  * Images\n  * RSS feed\n\n# The Gemini app becomes more agentic, delivering proactive, 24/7 help\n\nMay 19, 2026\n\n|\n\n6 min read\n\nGemini is becoming a more helpful AI assistant, with an intuitive new UI, proactive daily briefs and Gemini Spark, an agent to help you get things done around the clock.\n\nJosh Woodward VP, Google Labs, Gemini app & AI Studio\n\nIt’s been a banner year for the Gemini app. Last year at Google I/O, Gemini was serving 400 million users. Today, more than 900 million people across 230 countries and more than 70 languages turn to Gemini for help every month.\n\nIn time for Google I/O 2026, here’s what's new:\n\n  * Gemini 3.5 Flash: The first in our next generation of models that combines frontier intelligence with lightning-fast action.\n  * Neural Expressive: A vibrant, dynamic and completely reimagined design language for Gemini.\n  * Gemini Omni: Our new model that can seamlessly transform text, images and video prompts into cinematic, high-quality video outputs.\nAnd soon, we’ll start offering regional dialects, allowing you to choose a voice that truly resonates with you.\n\nFinally, we’re using the power of our Gemini models to make responses more engaging and easier to understand. Instead of throwing a wall of text at you, Gemini now designs tailored responses in real time — incorporating rich imagery, interactive timelines, narrated videos and dynamic graphics.\n\nNeural Expressive is rolling out globally today across the web, Android and iOS for everyone.\n\n## Gemini Omni: Turning your ideas into cinematic videos\n\nTo unlock your creative potential, we're introducing Gemini Omni, a model designed to turn your imagination into reality. By seamlessly combining text, images and video inputs, Gemini Omni allows you to generate stunning, high-quality video outputs effortlessly.\n\nWith Gemini Omni, video editing becomes a fluid, natural conversation. You can apply cinematic zooms or swap out backgrounds with a simple prompt. Just upload footage from your camera roll, apply built-in templates with a single tap and create polished content without expensive equipment or specialized technical jargon. You can even drop yourself directly into the action by creating a custom AI avatar that looks and sounds exactly like you.\n\nGemini Omni begins rolling out today to Google AI Plus, Pro and Ultra subscribers worldwide. ^{1}\n\n## Daily Brief: Start your day on the right foot\n\nWe’re introducing Daily Brief, an agent that gives you a personalized morning digest that’s designed to be your first stop every day. Built on the success of our recent Google Labs experiment CC, Daily Brief gives you a seamless, intuitive entry point into the world of AI agents.\n\nOnce you opt in, Gemini works across your connected apps in the background. It gathers urgent updates from your Gmail inbox, tracks upcoming events from your Calendar and compiles relevant follow-up details into a skimmable briefing.\n\nIt goes far beyond a simple summary. Daily Brief actively organizes and prioritizes based on your specific goals, even suggesting immediate next steps. You can easily steer it by giving responses a quick thumbs up or down over time.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nPresentamos Gemini Omni para Google Flow y Flow Music (https://blog.google/intl/es-419/actualizaciones-de-producto/flow-updates/)\nciteturn41126search4 [wordlim: 200] Published: 5 months ago; Crawled: 2 days ago; # Nuevos agentes, aplicaciones y Gemini Omni para Google Flow y Flow MusicMay 19, 2026\n\n# Nuevos agentes, aplicaciones y Gemini Omni para Google Flow y Flow Music\n\nMay 19, 2026\n\n|\n\n6 mins de lectura\n\nLas nuevas funciones de la familia de productos Google Flow te ayudan a imaginar, colaborar y perfeccionar tu proyecto en cada etapa.\n\nElias Roman\n\nVP, Product, Google Labs\n\nImage: Imagen con las palabras: amplifica tu visión y libera tu mejor trabajo\n\nEn el escenario de I/O del año pasado, presentamos Google Flow, una herramienta creada en colaboración con cineastas y pensada para ellos. Desde entonces, lo transformamos en un estudio creativo de IA, con nuevas funciones de generación y edición de imagen y video, y lo lanzamos en más de 140 países. A principios de este año, sumamos una nueva herramienta a la familia de Google Flow: Google Flow Music que ofrece el modelo de música más reciente de Google, Lyria 3 Pro, a artistas, productores y compositores. Ahora estamos incorporando un agente para cada etapa del proceso creativo, un nuevo modelo de IA que permite editar videos con precisión, la posibilidad de usar vibe coding para desarrollar flujos de trabajo personalizados y aplicaciones móviles para crear desde cualquier lugar.\n\nEstas son las novedades de Google Flow y Google Flow Music.\n\n## Novedades de Google Flow\n\nEstamos llevando Google Flow a otro nivel con Gemini Omni, una nueva experiencia basada en agentes y con herramientas personalizadas.\n\nAprovecha todo el potencial de Gemini Omni: Gemini Omni Flash es un modelo que puede crear contenido a partir de distintos formatos, empezando por videos. Combina la inteligencia de Gemini con nuestros modelos generativos de contenido multimedia y representa un salto en la comprensión del mundo, las capacidades multimodales y la edición precisa de video. Omni es como Nano Banana, pero para videos. Para los creativos que usan Google Flow, Omni Flash les permite combinar la inspiración del mundo real con contenido generado y refinar ideas\n\n  * Colabora en cada etapa: Google Flow Agent es tu socio creativo, capaz de planificar y abordar tareas complejas siguiendo tus indicaciones y bajo tu supervisión. Diseñado con modelos Gemini, aporta criterio y una comprensión profunda de tu proyecto para ayudarte con la generación inicial de ideas, la creación y la edición. Por ejemplo, este agente puede ayudarte a probar diálogos entre personajes en una escena específica o incluso sugerirte ideas para la trama. Cuando hayas avanzado más en un proyecto, el agente puede crear diversas variantes al mismo tiempo para darte más opciones o incluso editar por lotes para que tus ajustes se reflejen en todos los recursos. Una vez que tus recursos estén listos, el agente puede organizarlos en colecciones y renombrarlos de forma intuitiva. Este agente ya está disponible para todos los usuarios de Google Flow a nivel global.\n\n  * Crea lo que necesites con herramientas personalizadas: Gracias a Google Flow Tools, ahora puedes usar lenguaje natural para crear herramientas y flujos de trabajo a medida dentro de Google Flow. Ya sea que busques un editor de imágenes en particular, una herramienta para cambiar el tamaño de los videos o sombreadores personalizados, ahora puedes crearlos fácilmente sin necesidad de saber programar. Además, si creas algo que piensas que otras personas podrían disfrutar, puedes compartir tu herramienta con otros usuarios de Flow, que pueden adaptarla a su gusto. Por ejemplo, uno de nuestros socios con acceso anticipado, László Gaal, creó una herramienta llamada “pixelBento” para aplicar efectos de posproducción como estéticas lo-fi o glitch. Descubre esta herramienta y muchas más en Flow, incluidas algunas creadas por nuestros socios Kat Zhang y metapuppet. Los usuarios de Flow en todo el mundo pueden usar las herramientas existentes, y los suscriptores de Google AI también pueden crearlas y modificarlas.\n\n## Novedades de Google Flow Music\n\nGoogle Flow Music siempre te permitió crear, iterar y compartir canciones con calidad de estudio. Nuestras funciones más recientes ofrecen un control de edición más potente y una mejor creación de videos musicales.\n\nSorry, your browser doesn't support embedded videos, but don't worry, you can download it and watch it with your favorite video player!\n\n  * Edita tu canción con precisión, sección por sección: Ahora, artistas, compositores y productores tienen un control más detallado sobre lo que crean en Google Flow Music. Puedes seleccionar cualquier parte de una canción y modificarla. Reescribe o traduce letras al instante, cambia el estilo del ritmo y mucho más, sin alterar el resto de la pista. También puedes tomar un fragmento específico de una de tus canciones y desarrollarlo en una dirección completamente nueva.\n  * Reimagina tus temas completos con versiones cover: Transforma el estilo de las canciones que hayas hecho en Google Flow Music, manteniendo la melodía y la estructura original. Por ejemplo, prueba con una versión “lo-fi para estudiar” de tu playlist favorita.\n  * Crea videos musicales con Gemini Omni: Nuestro modelo más reciente llega también a Google Flow Music, lo que te permite dirigir videos musicales conversando con el agente y luego compartirlos. Con Omni Flash puedes guiar los estilos, los protagonistas y las escenas para que acompañen la narrativa y el ritmo de tu tema. Disponible para suscriptores de Google AI\n\nPor último, estamos lanzando las aplicaciones de Google Flow y Google Flow Music para dispositivos móviles. Las versiones web seguirán siendo las plataformas principales para acceder a todas las funciones, pero las nuevas aplicaciones brindan flexibilidad para crear desde cualquier lugar. Para usuarios mayores de 18 años, la aplicación de Flow está disponible en Android en versión beta (próximamente en iOS) y la aplicación de Flow Music ya está disponible en iOS (próximamente en Android).\n\nMillones de creativos de las más diversas disciplinas dieron vida a sus ideas con Google Flow y Google Flow Music durante el último año. Tenemos muchas ganas de ver qué surge con estas nuevas funciones en manos de la comunidad creativa.\n\nPublicado en:\n\n  * Google Labs--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nEgoBabyVLM: Benchmarking Cross-Modal Learning from Naturalistic Egocentric Video Data (https://arxiv.org/abs/2605.19130)\nciteturn41126academia11 [wordlim: 200] Published: 5 months ago; To motivate progress, we introduce the EgoBabyVLM Challenge to drive the development of models capable of grounded language learning from the kind of naturalistic data that human infants experience.\nTitle: EgoBabyVLM: Benchmarking Cross-Modal Learning from Naturalistic Egocentric Video Data\nAuthors: Dongyan Lin, Phillip Rust, Angel Villar Corrales, Alvin W. M. Tan, Mahi Luthra, Charles-Éric Saint-James, Rashel Moritz, Sheila Krogh-Jespersen, Vanessa Stark, Surya Parimi, Jiayi Shen, Youssef Benchekroun, Yosuke Higuchi, Martin Gleize, Tom Fizycki, Nicolas Hamilakis, Manel Khentout, Sho Tsuji, Balázs Kégl, Juan Pino, Michael C. Frank, Emmanuel Dupoux\nDate: Mon May 18 21:30:54 2026\n\nChildren acquire language grounding with remarkable robustness from limited visuo-linguistic input in ways that surpass today's best large multimodal models. Recent research suggests current vision-language models (VLMs) trained on curated web data fail to generalize to the sparse, weakly-aligned egocentric streams produced by wearable devices, embodied agents, and infant head-cams -- and no fixed evaluation pipeline exists for measuring progress on this regime. We train VLMs on datasets with varying degrees of semantic alignment between visual and linguistic inputs, including naturalistic infant and adult egocentric videos, and evaluate them with a comprehensive suite spanning multimodal language grounding and unimodal vision and language tasks. At the core of this suite is Machine-DevBench, a corpus-grounded benchmark of lexical and grammatical competence, automatically generated from the model's training vocabulary across logarithmic frequency bins to eliminate the train/eval mismatch and low statistical power of prior developmental benchmarks. Our results show that current VLM paradigms hinge on the tight semantic alignment of curated data and fail to exploit the weakly-aligned signal that dominates naturalistic egocentric input -- the very regime in which humans thrive. To motivate progress, we introduce the EgoBabyVLM Challenge to drive the development of models capable of grounded language learning from the kind of naturalistic data that human infants experience.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nGoogle I/O 2026: Sundar Pichai’s opening keynote (https://blog.google/intl/en-africa/products/explore-get-answers/sundar-pichai-io-2026/?hl=en-GB)\nciteturn41126search5 [wordlim: 200] Published: 5 months ago; Crawled: today; May 19, 2026 ...   * Gemini for Science brings together a number of AI tools to help accelerate scientific research.\n\n# I/O 2026: Welcome to the agentic Gemini era\n\nMay 19, 2026\n\n|\n\nHere’s how we’re helping you get more done with Gemini.\n\nSundar Pichai\n\nCEO of Google and Alphabet\n\nImage: a series of colorful icons representing Google I/O against a black background\n\nEditor’s note: Below is an edited transcript of Google CEO Sundar Pichai’s remarks at Google I/O 2026, adapted to include more of what was announced on stage. See all the announcements in our collection.\n\nIt’s been an extraordinary year since our last I/O, a period of relentless shipping, technology advances and hyper progress. We’re now in the part of the AI cycle where people want to see the value in the products they use every day. We’ve been really focused on that, and you’ll see that in the products and features we’re announcing today at I/O.\n\nTen years since we pivoted the company to be AI-first, we still see AI as the most profound way to advance our mission and improve people’s lives at scale.That’s why we’ve been taking a differentiated, full-stack approach to AI innovation, from our custom silicon and secure foundation, to our world-class research and models, to our products and platforms that touch billions of people. --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nGoogle I/O 2026: Discurso inaugural de Sundar Pichai (https://blog.google/intl/es-419/noticias-de-la-empresa/tecnologia/sundar-pichai-io-2026/)\nciteturn41126search6 [wordlim: 200] Published: 5 months ago; Crawled: today; May 19, 2026 ... ## Gemini Omni\n\n# I/O 2026: Bienvenido a la era de Gemini impulsada por agentes\n\nMay 19, 2026\n\n|\n\nDescubre cómo te ayudamos a aumentar tu productividad con Gemini.\n\nSundar Pichai\n\nCEO of Google and Alphabet\n\nImage: a series of colorful icons representing Google I/O against a black background\n\nTemas en este artículo\n\n* * *\n\n  * El impulso de la IA y los productos\n  * IA conversacional\n  * Infraestructura e innovación\n  * Modelos de Gemini\n  * Agentes\n  * Más sobre la era de Gemini con agentes\n\nNota del editor: A continuación, presentamos una transcripción editada de los comentarios de Sundar Pichai, director general de Google, en Google I/O 2026, adaptada para incluir más de los anuncios que se hicieron en el escenario. Consulta todos los anuncios en nuestra colección.\n\nDesde la última edición de I/O, vivimos un año extraordinario, lleno de lanzamientos, avances tecnológicos y un progreso muy acelerado. Llegamos a una etapa del ciclo de la IA en la que las personas quieren ver su valor en los productos que usan todos los días. ## El impulso de nuestros productos\n\nHoy tenemos 13 productos con más de mil millones de usuarios cada uno. Cinco de ellos tienen más de 3 mil millones de usuarios.\nNuestros modelos de Gemini son una de las principales razones por las que cada vez más personas eligen nuestros productos y los usan con más frecuencia.\n\nTodo comienza con el Buscador, que lleva los beneficios de la IA generativa a más personas que cualquier otro producto en el mundo. Visión general creada por IA ya tiene más de 2,500 millones de usuarios activos mensuales. Además, Modo IA fue toda una revelación: nuestra mayor actualización del Buscador hasta la fecha. A las personas les encanta y, en solo un año, ya superó los mil millones de usuarios activos mensuales.\n\nCuando las personas prueban las funciones basadas en IA del Buscador, lo usan más. El Buscador pasó de centrarse en consultas individuales a sentirse más como una conversación continua que te ofrece información más detallada y te conecta con la inmensidad de la Web.\n\n  * TPU 8t está optimizado para el preentrenamiento a gran escala y ofrece casi el triple de potencia de procesamiento básica que la generación anterior. También replanteamos por completo nuestra infraestructura de entrenamiento. Con JAX y Pathways, el entrenamiento ya no está limitado a un único gran centro de datos. Ahora, podemos distribuirlo sin interrupciones en varios sitios y escalarlo a más de un millón de TPUs en todo el mundo, lo que nos permite tener el mayor clúster de entrenamiento del mundo. Para quienes crean modelos, eso significa entrenar modelos más grandes y capaces en semanas en lugar de meses.\n  * TPU 8i está diseñado para tareas de inferencia. Mejoramos de forma drástica la velocidad en cada paso porque, si hay algo que aprendimos durante 27 años de trabajo en el Buscador, es que la latencia importa.\n\nAdemás de la velocidad, también pensamos en cómo escalar de forma sustentable. Ambos chips tienen mayor eficiencia energética y ofrecen hasta el doble de rendimiento por watt.\n\n## Gemini Omni\n\nEste progreso con las TPUs nos permite impulsar avances de procesamiento en modelos, programación y agentes. Con los modelos de mundo, la IA está pasando de predecir texto a simular la realidad. Trabajamos para ampliar los límites de lo que pueden hacer estos modelos.\n\nGemini Omni es nuestro nuevo modelo capaz de generar muestras en cualquier modalidad de salida a partir de cualquier dato de entrada. Empezamos con resultados de video y, con el tiempo, habilitaremos imágenes y texto. Este nuevo modelo combina la inteligencia de Gemini con nuestros modelos generativos de contenido multimedia, un gran salto en la comprensión del mundo. Ahora, lanzamos el primer modelo de la familia Omni: Gemini Omni Flash.\n\nGemini Omni Flash está disponible a partir de hoy. Podrás probarlo en la aplicación Gemini, Google Flow y YouTube Shorts. Durante las próximas semanas, también lo lanzaremos para desarrolladores y clientes empresariales mediante APIs.\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nGoogle AI subscription updates from Google I/O 2026 (https://blog.google/products-and-platforms/products/google-one/google-ai-subscriptions/)\nciteturn41126search7 [wordlim: 200] Published: 5 months ago; Crawled: last month; May 19, 2026 ... And in Google Flow, our AI creative studio, Gemini Omni allows you to blend real-world inspiration with generated content and iterate conversationally.\n\n# Everything new in our Google AI subscriptions, fresh from I/O 2026\n\nMay 19, 2026\n\n|\n\nIntroducing a $100 AI Ultra plan — plus, new features and benefits for AI Plus, Pro and Ultra subscribers.\n\n* * *\n\nShimrit Ben-Yair VP, Google Photos, Google One & AI Subscriptions\n\n* * *\n\nImage: The image shows colorful icons. The copy reads: More magic in one plan. More power, more perks, same price.\n\nYour browser does not support the audio element.\n\nListen to article\n\n[[duration]] minutes\n\nThis content is generated by Google AI. Generative AI is experimental\n\n[Input]\n\nVoice Speed\n\nVoice\n\nSpeed 0.75X 1X 1.5X 2X\n\nWe’re redefining what AI can do — and a Google AI subscription is your VIP pass to experience all of it. Our AI subs offer premium benefits across Google, extra storage and tools to boost your productivity and creativity.\n\nHere are all the AI subscription updates we shared at Google I/O 2026.\n\n## A new $100 AI Ultra plan\n\nWe’re launching a $100/month AI Ultra plan, specifically tailored for developers, technical leads, knowledge workers and advanced creators. \n## Access to our latest models\n\nWith an AI subscription, you get access to our latest models, including:\n\n  * Gemini Omni (AI Plus, Pro and Ultra; global): Gemini Omni is our new model that can create anything from any input, starting with video. It combines Gemini’s intelligence with our generative media models for a new level of world understanding, multimodality and editing. Omni in the Gemini app helps you bring your ideas to life, using any combination of text, images and video inputs. It’s never been so easy to create and edit videos. You can upload any photo or video from your camera roll, apply built-in templates with a single click and experience the magic without needing expensive equipment or technical jargon. And in Google Flow, our AI creative studio, Gemini Omni allows you to blend real-world inspiration with generated content and iterate conversationally. It also improves character consistency, meaning identity and voice are preserved across every scene.\n\n  * Gemini 3.5 Flash (AI Plus, Pro and Ultra; global): Gemini 3.5 Flash delivers frontier performance for agents and coding, excelling at complex long-horizon tasks that deliver real-world utility.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nGoogle I/O 2026: Sundar Pichai’s opening keynote (https://blog.google/intl/en-nz/company-news/sundar-pichai-io-2026/)\nciteturn41126search8 [wordlim: 200] Published: 5 months ago; Crawled: today; ## Gemini Omni ... Gemini Omni is our new model that is capable of generating samples in any output modality from any input.\nWe’ve taken a fundamentally different approach with our training infrastructure. With JAX and Pathways, our training is no longer constrained by the limits of a single, massive data center. Instead, we can now seamlessly distribute training across multiple sites, scaling training across more than 1 million TPUs globally. This gives us the ability to create the largest training cluster in the world. For model builders, this means training larger, more capable models in weeks rather than months.\n  * TPU 8i is designed for inference. We have dramatically improved speed at every step. Because if we learned anything in 27 years of working on Search, it's that latency matters.\n\nIn addition to speed, we’re also thinking about scaling sustainably. Both chips are more energy efficient, delivering up to two times better performance-per-watt.\n\n## Gemini Omni\n\nThis progress with TPUs is how we can make compute advances across models, coding and agents. With world models, AI is moving from predicting text to simulating reality. We have been working to push the boundaries of what these models can do.\n\nGemini Omni is our new model that is capable of generating samples in any output modality from any input. We’re starting with video outputs, and over time we’ll enable image and text. This new model combines Gemini’s intelligence with our generative media models — a huge leap forward in world understanding. We’re launching the first model in the Omni family: Gemini Omni Flash.\n\nGemini Omni Flash is available starting today. You will be able to try it on the Gemini app, Google Flow and on YouTube Shorts. We'll also be rolling it out to developers and enterprise customers via APIs in the coming weeks.\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nTech Blog (https://seed.bytedance.com/en/blog_list/foundation)\nciteturn41126search9 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Jun 19, 2026 ... May 19, 2025\n\n# Blog/Foundation models\n\n[Input: Search][Button: Search]\n\nCategory\n\nNewest → oldest\n\nJun 23, 2026\n\nSeed2.1 Officially Released: Advancing AI Productivity Enhanced agent & coding capabilities for reliable delivery in complex scenarios.\n\nJun 19, 2026\n\nSeed-2.1-Preview Model Release on Arena\n\nFeb 16, 2026\n\nDola-Seed-2.0-Preview Model Release on Arena\n\nFeb 14, 2026\n\nSeed 2.0 Official Launch A breakthrough in real-world complex task execution.\n\nDec 24, 2025\n\nSeed Prover 1.5: Advanced Mathematical Reasoning through a Novel Agentic Architecture Solved 11 problems of the 2025 Putnam competition in just 9 hours.\n\nDec 18, 2025\n\nOfficial Release of Seed1.8: A Generalized Agentic Model An all-in-one integration of search, coding, and GUI Agent capabilities.\n\nAug 21, 2025\n\nSeed-OSS Open-Source Models Release Native long context window and flexible control of thinking budget.\n\nJul 31, 2025\n\nSeed Research￨Seed Diffusion Preview Released: A Diffusion Language Model Delivering Breakthrough 2,146 Tokens/s Inference Speed Over 100 lines of code can be generated within one second.\n\nJun 28, 2025\n\nBuilt on Seed1.6-Flash, Seed-1.6-Embedding Launched It stands out with multimodal hybrid retrieval, SOTA performance and flexibility.\n\nJun 25, 2025\n\nIntroduction to Techniques Used in Seed1.6 Adaptive thinking powered by multimodal capabilities (Including college entrance examination scores).\n\nMay 19, 2025\n\nSeed-Coder Open-Sourced: LLM-Based Code Data Building Method Validated The data pipeline and BF16 precision version are now available for download.\n\nMay 13, 2025\n\nFirst Release of Seed VLM Tech Report: Comprehensive Solutions for Image, Video, GUI, and Game Achieves SOTA on 38 Benchmarks."
